Mark the restarts of playout and recording for another device chosen in a call

WebRTC patch 0014 aligns the echo controller again when the audio device module starts
recording again by itself while it records (MarkAudioDeviceRestarted), and the macOS
engine device marks its restarts (apple patch 0010). On Linux and Windows the wrapper's
AudioDeviceImpl restarts the streams itself when another output or input is chosen while
they run (patch 0021): the output stops and starts again on the other device, and what is
played reaches the microphone along another path, maybe with another delay; or recording
stops and starts again on the other input. The audio state starts neither, so nothing
told the echo controller. AudioDeviceImpl now marks a restart after the output started
again on another device while recording runs, and after recording started again on
another input; not when the output is chosen while nothing records, nor when a start
fails. A change of devices is marked as before (patch 0021), so the next recorded block
follows patch 0014's rule for it.

Not marked here: PulseAudio's own restarts of its streams (the sound server back, the
chosen device back) and a stream the server moves to another device, which WebRTC patch
0015 marks in the device module. Windows' Core Audio module starts nothing again by
itself while recording runs: a change of the default device leaves its streams where they
were opened.

test/echo_call.test.cc: with the mock audio device, the output chosen again while
recording runs marks one restart, recording chosen again on another input another; the
output chosen with nothing recording, or with nothing playing or recording, marks none.

diff --git a/src/rtc_audio_device_impl.cc b/src/rtc_audio_device_impl.cc
index a5a3c7b..6e0821a 100644
--- a/src/rtc_audio_device_impl.cc
+++ b/src/rtc_audio_device_impl.cc
@@ -67,7 +67,13 @@ int32_t AudioDeviceImpl::SetPlayoutDevice(uint16_t index) {
       audio_device_module_->StopPlayout();
       audio_device_module_->SetPlayoutDevice(index);
       audio_device_module_->InitPlayout();
-      audio_device_module_->StartPlayout();
+      // Fogata: what is played now reaches the microphone along another path, maybe
+      // with another delay: while recording runs, the echo controller aligns again
+      // (WebRTC patch 0014).
+      if (audio_device_module_->StartPlayout() == 0 &&
+          audio_device_module_->Recording()) {
+        webrtc::MarkAudioDeviceRestarted();
+      }
     } else {
       audio_device_module_->SetPlayoutDevice(index);
     }
@@ -87,7 +93,12 @@ int32_t AudioDeviceImpl::SetRecordingDevice(uint16_t index) {
       audio_device_module_->StopRecording();
       audio_device_module_->SetRecordingDevice(index);
       audio_device_module_->InitRecording();
-      audio_device_module_->StartRecording();
+      // Fogata: recording started again by the device, not by the audio state, which
+      // aligns the echo controller only as it starts recording itself (WebRTC patch
+      // 0014).
+      if (audio_device_module_->StartRecording() == 0) {
+        webrtc::MarkAudioDeviceRestarted();
+      }
     } else {
       audio_device_module_->SetRecordingDevice(index);
     }
diff --git a/test/echo_call.test.cc b/test/echo_call.test.cc
index a6af670..418c02f 100644
--- a/test/echo_call.test.cc
+++ b/test/echo_call.test.cc
@@ -561,3 +561,46 @@ TEST_F(EchoCall, ADeviceRestartWhileRecordingAlignsItAgain) {
   state_->RemoveSendingStream(&voice_);
   state_->RemoveReceivingStream(&heard_);
 }
+
+// The wrapper marks a restart (MarkAudioDeviceRestarted, WebRTC patch 0014) when it
+// starts the output again on another device while recording runs, and when it starts
+// recording again on another input; not when the output is chosen while recording
+// does not run, nor when nothing plays or records.
+TEST(EchoCallDevices, ARestartWhileRecordingIsMarked) {
+  auto worker = webrtc::Thread::Create();
+  worker->Start();
+  auto adm = webrtc::test::MockAudioDeviceModule::CreateNice();
+  bool playing = false;
+  bool recording = false;
+  ON_CALL(*adm, Playing()).WillByDefault([&] { return playing; });
+  ON_CALL(*adm, Recording()).WillByDefault([&] { return recording; });
+  ON_CALL(*adm, StartPlayout()).WillByDefault(Return(0));
+  ON_CALL(*adm, StartRecording()).WillByDefault(Return(0));
+  {
+    libwebrtc::scoped_refptr<libwebrtc::AudioDeviceImpl> device(
+        new libwebrtc::RefCountedObject<libwebrtc::AudioDeviceImpl>(
+            adm, worker.get()));
+    auto restarts = [] { return webrtc::AudioDeviceRestartsCount().load(); };
+    auto settle = [&] { worker->BlockingCall([] {}); };
+
+    uint64_t before = restarts();
+    device->SetPlayoutDevice(1);
+    device->SetRecordingDevice(1);
+    settle();
+    EXPECT_EQ(restarts(), before) << "nothing plays or records";
+
+    playing = true;
+    device->SetPlayoutDevice(2);
+    settle();
+    EXPECT_EQ(restarts(), before) << "playing, not recording";
+
+    recording = true;
+    device->SetPlayoutDevice(3);
+    settle();
+    EXPECT_EQ(restarts(), before + 1) << "the output again while recording";
+    device->SetRecordingDevice(2);
+    settle();
+    EXPECT_EQ(restarts(), before + 2) << "recording again on another input";
+  }
+  worker->Stop();
+}
